<pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.14" change_id="I71208a75a11946181588478e3c86d91fc064ddf4" commit="ff7e685f93ef43131a7edf3a1f70cc8e11fe5f64" commit_message="CHROMIUM: rockchip: support prime fd import  The prime fd to handle ioctl was not used with rockchip before. Support was added in order to pass graphics_Gbm and to support potential uses within Chrome OS (e.g. zero-copy video decode, camera).  TEST=graphics_Gbm BUG=chromium:575734  Change-Id: I71208a75a11946181588478e3c86d91fc064ddf4 Signed-off-by: Zach Reizner &lt;zachr@google.com&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/323854 Commit-Ready: Zach Reizner &lt;zachr@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Zach Reizner &lt;zachr@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Daniel Kurtz &lt;djkurtz@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="1" gerrit_number="323854" owner_email="zachr@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="8" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/54/323854/8" remote="cros" total_fail_count="1"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.14" change_id="Icfa765e0345c698a4fbdce036e2fd3b6a7017c5e" commit="d9573db1585b55328ec7c0f61df03382c99671b9" commit_message="CHROMIUM: alt-syscall: Whitelist tkill() for Android  tkill(2) is used by strace.  BUG=b:26865128,b:26589008 TEST=Builds for Oak and Cyan.  Change-Id: Icfa765e0345c698a4fbdce036e2fd3b6a7017c5e Signed-off-by: Andrew Bresticker &lt;abrestic@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/324627 Reviewed-by: Luigi Semenzato &lt;semenzato@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="324627" owner_email="abrestic@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/27/324627/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.18" change_id="Ic3c87656a4e37ca69422aac1a0881d49d8006921" commit="1f7670a765c5ee484d3f40877215ed2742d3e9d6" commit_message="CHROMIUM: clk: Fix out-of-bounds read in clk_notifier_register()  If the struct clk_notifier corresponding to the given struct clk is not found in the global clk_notifier_list, cn will not point to a valid struct clk_notifier.  Use a temporary to iterate over the list and only set cn if the matching struct clk_notifier is found.  BUG=chromium:581371 TEST=Build and boot on Smaug.  Change-Id: Ic3c87656a4e37ca69422aac1a0881d49d8006921 Signed-off-by: Andrew Bresticker &lt;abrestic@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/323838 Reviewed-by: Benson Leung &lt;bleung@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Alexander Potapenko &lt;glider@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="323838" owner_email="abrestic@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/38/323838/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Iea0abc378e13ddb77b274246cd1a470747b83647" commit="aca22ec747fcc5d181091d515a4549d745d2f63b" commit_message="servo v3: add atmega pty  Add servod and xml hooks for uart4 routed to the atmega USB keyboard emulator on servo v3. Allow usbkm232 init after other gpio init to preserve settings. Ensure USB routing is correct.  BUG=chromium:551926 TEST=servod --board=panther --usbkm232=atmega &amp;; dut-control kb_press:d_key  Change-Id: Iea0abc378e13ddb77b274246cd1a470747b83647 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/317120 Commit-Ready: Nick Sanders &lt;nsanders@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Nick Sanders &lt;nsanders@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Richard Barnette &lt;jrbarnette@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Todd Broch &lt;tbroch@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="317120" owner_email="nsanders@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/third_party/hdctools" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/hdctools" ref="refs/changes/20/317120/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.14" change_id="I6eb03d3a0ae64ca547b7e7f210417eee25a92939" commit="b1c81906bb20591c03bb4f102d747323dbad0d77" commit_message="FROMLIST: usb: dwc2: host: There's not really a TT for the root hub  I find that when I plug a full speed (NOT high speed) hub into a dwc2 port and then I plug a bunch of devices into that full speed hub that dwc2 goes bat guano crazy.  Specifically, it just spews errors like this in the console:   usb usb1: clear tt 1 (9043) error -22  The specific test case I used looks like this: /:  Bus 01.Port 1: Dev 1, Class=root_hub, Driver=dwc2/1p, 480M     |__ Port 1: Dev 17, If 0, Class=Hub, Driver=hub/4p, 12M         |__ Port 2: Dev 19, If 0, ..., Driver=usbhid, 1.5M         |__ Port 4: Dev 20, If 0, ..., Driver=usbhid, 12M         |__ Port 4: Dev 20, If 1, ..., Driver=usbhid, 12M         |__ Port 4: Dev 20, If 2, ..., Driver=usbhid, 12M  Showing VID/PID:  Bus 001 Device 001: ID 1d6b:0002 Linux Foundation 2.0 root hub  Bus 001 Device 017: ID 03eb:3301 Atmel Corp. at43301 4-Port Hub  Bus 001 Device 020: ID 045e:0745 Microsoft Corp. Nano Transceiver ...  Bus 001 Device 019: ID 046d:c404 Logitech, Inc. TrackMan Wheel  I spent a bunch of time trying to figure out why there are errors to begin with.  I believe that the issue may be a hardware issue where the transceiver sometimes accidentally sends a PREAMBLE packet if you send a packet to a full speed device right after one to a low speed device. Luckily the USB driver retries and the second time things work OK.  In any case, things kinda seem work despite the errors, except for the &quot;clear tt&quot; spew mucking up my console.  Chalk it up for a win for retries and robust protocols.  So getting back to the &quot;clear tt&quot; problem, it appears that we get those because there's not actually a TT here to clear.  It's my understanding that when dwc2 operates in low speed or full speed mode that there's no real TT out there.  That makes all these attempts to &quot;clear the TT&quot; somewhat meaningless and also causes the spew in the log.  Let's just skip all the useless TT clears.  Eventually we should root cause the errors, but even if we do this is still a proper fix and is likely to avoid the &quot;clear tt&quot; error in the future.  Note that hooking up a Full Speed USB Audio Device (Jabra 510) to this same hub with the keyboard / trackball shows that even audio works over this janky connection.  As a point to note, this particular change (skip bogus TT clears) compared to just commenting out the dev_err() in hub_tt_work() actually produces better audio.  Note: don't ask me where I got a full speed USB hub or whether the massive amount of dust that accumulated on it while it was in my junk box affected its funtionality.  Just smile and nod.  BUG=chrome-os-partner:49855 TEST=No more console spew  Change-Id: I6eb03d3a0ae64ca547b7e7f210417eee25a92939 Signed-off-by: Douglas Anderson &lt;dianders@chromium.org&gt; (am from https://patchwork.kernel.org/patch/8157731/) Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/323773 Reviewed-by: Julius Werner &lt;jwerner@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="323773" owner_email="dianders@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="3" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/73/323773/3" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I676bc3fe2edf6aa1da6a4f82d615a8d3e3b703e7" commit="f97e4c560652ca72ae2f29afe5e4be4fd4fa06a2" commit_message="Add JOB_RETRIES = 2 to tests  BUG=None TEST=None  Change-Id: I676bc3fe2edf6aa1da6a4f82d615a8d3e3b703e7 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/324790 Commit-Ready: Kalin Stoyanov &lt;kalin@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Kalin Stoyanov &lt;kalin@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Sridhar Sonti &lt;sontis@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Wai-Hong Tam &lt;waihong@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="324790" owner_email="kalin@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/autotest" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/autotest" ref="refs/changes/90/324790/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.18" change_id="Icfa765e0345c698a4fbdce036e2fd3b6a7017c5e" commit="c4db18f63c2e8f4361047cef9aa7c62f62416f7e" commit_message="CHROMIUM: alt-syscall: Whitelist tkill() for Android  tkill(2) is used by strace.  BUG=b:26865128,b:26589008 TEST=Builds for Oak and Cyan.  Change-Id: Icfa765e0345c698a4fbdce036e2fd3b6a7017c5e Signed-off-by: Andrew Bresticker &lt;abrestic@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/324791 Reviewed-by: Luigi Semenzato &lt;semenzato@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="324791" owner_email="abrestic@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/91/324791/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.18" change_id="I1a1da18175ad2fdb11116246cf8f1f884f5ec879" commit="9ca5721f9676f3f8fd71dd4beadc3613716aa1dc" commit_message="CHROMIUM: usb: gadget: configfs: fix panic in android_disconnect  This change prevents a NULL pointer access kernel panic when udc driver calls configfs gadget driver's disconnect() after the configfs gadget driver has already unbound.  BUG=chrome-os-partner:47236 TEST=run 'mtp-detect' on Ubuntu host with Smaug connected as SS, and observe no kernel panic anymore  Change-Id: I1a1da18175ad2fdb11116246cf8f1f884f5ec879 Signed-off-by: Henry Lin &lt;henryl@nvidia.com&gt; Signed-off-by: Mark Kuo &lt;mkuo@nvidia.com&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/324686 Commit-Ready: Andrew Bresticker &lt;abrestic@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Jim Lin &lt;jilin@nvidia.com&gt; Reviewed-by: Jim Lin &lt;jilin@nvidia.com&gt; Reviewed-by: Andrew Bresticker &lt;abrestic@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="324686" owner_email="mkuo@nvidia.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/86/324686/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I4a2bf028275db57b2d0469fc1cb574e871820713" commit="d44885120cfe8dcceaaa43f98a0de26a00db68ea" commit_message="vboot_display: Keep track of displayed screen  Vboot needs to track the currently displayed screen so when it needs to change the locale or display the debug overlay it knows which screen to redraw.  Currently only the legacy path is doing this so change the new path to update the current screen if it is successfully drawn.  BUG=chrome-os-partner:49766 BRANCH=glados TEST=boot on glados in dev mode, hit tab and ensure screen does not go black  Change-Id: I4a2bf028275db57b2d0469fc1cb574e871820713 Signed-off-by: Duncan Laurie &lt;dlaurie@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/324549 Reviewed-by: Aaron Durbin &lt;adurbin@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="324549" owner_email="dlaurie@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/platform/vboot_reference" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/vboot_reference" ref="refs/changes/49/324549/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><lkgm version="7876.0.0-rc2"/></manifest>